# Verification

These rules apply before an AI agent reports any work as finished.

- Run the checks the repository already provides — its test suite, linter,
  formatter, and pre-commit hooks — and name the ones that were run.
- Never bypass a check to make a commit land: no `--no-verify`, no skipping
  hooks, and no disabling a lint rule to silence a warning instead of fixing
  the code behind it.
- Report results faithfully. If a test fails, say so and include the relevant
  output. If a check was skipped or could not run, say that too, and why.
- "It should work" is not verification. Either a check ran, or the work is
  reported as unverified.
- When something cannot be verified automatically, state exactly what the user
  has to do to confirm it.
- Finish the whole task before reporting. If part of it is blocked, complete
  everything else and say plainly what was left out and why.
